  "id": "perceptual-measure",
  "term": "perceptual measure",
  "definition": "A perceptual measure is a way of judging image quality by how human observers actually perceive a change, rather than only by numerical calculations. In this source, it refers to an objective performance-based measure based on detection thresholds, such as how much noise remains visible to a person after image processing.",
